{"ts": 1789783112.4565902, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "## Summary\n\n**Submitted:** long features 7, 9, and 15, equal weight. In-sample Sharpe **0.972**. Predicted OOS Sharpe: **0.65 \u00b1 0.30**.\n\n**How I got there:**\n\nI scanned all 40 features individually, then built up combinations. Feature 7 was the standout (0.760 solo), with 9 and 15 the best partners.\n\n**The key diagnostic** was testing triples of *mediocre* features as a control. Those returned 0.26\u20130.46, not ~0.93. That ruled out the possibility that the high scores were just a mechanical \u221ak diversification artifact \u2014 something I'd initially suspected when every partner of feature 7 landed in a narrow band around its solo value. The control showed the selected features carry real signal.\n\n**Sign-flip tests confirmed causality.** Reversing feature 7 collapsed the spec from 0.972 to 0.096 \u2014 decisive. Flipping 9 or 15 cost ~0.53 each, far beyond noise. All three features are genuinely predictive with the signs I chose.\n\n**Why I predict 0.65, not 0.97:**\n\nThe in-sample number is the maximum of ~56 evaluations, and I'm submitting the winner. Three corrections apply:\n\n- **Selection bias** \u2014 the ~10 genuinely-good triples I found clustered at 0.85\u20130.97. That cluster's center (~0.92) is a fairer estimate of this family's quality than its peak, which caught a favorable draw.\n- **Winner's curse on components** \u2014 features 9 and 15 were the 2nd/3rd best of 80 signed singles, so their 0.47/0.45 solo scores are likely inflated; their true edge is probably nearer 0.3.\n- **Structural decay** \u2014 equal weighting helps here (no fitted weights to overfit), but in-sample correlation structure still shifts OOS.\n\nThe sd of 0.30 reflects sampling error (~0.22 at n=5000) plus genuine uncertainty about how much of the edge survives. It spans a disappointing ~0.1 through a strong ~1.2.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: the biggest risk isn't that the features are fake \u2014 the sign-flip evidence is strong \u2014 but that my *point estimate* of their strength is inflated by having picked the best of many. If anything, 0.65 may still be slightly optimistic."}
